|passage={{...}} we remember once hearing a '''fast''' man suggest that they were evidently "nobs who had overdrawn the badger by driving fast cattle, and going it high" — the exact signification of which words we did not understand {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=The Herald of Health and Journal of Physical Culture| volume=I| year=1867| title=Temperance and its Champions| author=George W. Bungay| page=277| url=https://books.google.be/books?id=eyagAAAAMAAJ&pg=RA1-PA277&dq=%22the+unenviable+reputation+of+being+a+fast+man%22&hl=en&sa=X&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22the%20unenviable%20reputation%20of%20being%20a%20fast%20man%22&f=false| passage=Had Senator Wilson won the unenviable reputation of being a ''fast'' man—a lover of wine, or had he shown himself to the public in a state of inebriety, unable to stand erect in Fanueil Hall for instance, leaning upon the desk to “maintain the center of gravity,” and uttering words that fell sprawling in “muddy obscurity” from lips redolent of rum, rendering it necessary for a prompter and an interpreter to sculpture his speech into symmetry for the public ear and the public press, he would have been pelted from his high office with the indignant ballots of his constituents.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1933|author=w:Dorothy L. Sayers|title=The Queen’s Square|passage=“I don’t like that young woman,” said Lady Hermione; she’s '''fast'''.” “Dear Lady!” “I’ve no doubt you think me old-fashioned. Well, I’m glad I am. I say she’s '''fast''', and what’s more, heartless. I was watching her before supper, and I’m sorry for Tony Lee. She’s been flirting as hard as she can go with Harry Vibart-not to give it a worse name-and she’s got Jim Playfair on a string too. She can’t even leave Frank Bellingham alone, though she’s staying in his house.”}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1979|author=w:Doug Fieger|title={{w|Good Girls Don't (song)|Good Girls Don't}}
|passage=You're alone with her at last / And you're waiting 'til you think the time is right / Cause you've heard she's pretty '''fast''' / And you're hoping that she'll give you some tonight.}}
