#* {{quote-book|en|title=A Novelist on Novels|author=w:Walter Lionel George|year=1918|url=https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/32576/pg32576-images.html|passage={{...}} if she is of the slightly '''faster''' kind that gives smart lunch parties at the Strand Corner House, her diet is sometimes a little stronger; she takes to novels of the orchid house and the tiger's lair, to the artless erotics of Miss Elinor Glyn, Mr Hubert Wales, and Miss Victoria Cross.}}
